                        "entry_id": "2adbe30c-0365-3cda-b952-ba93225e042b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A cry of impassioned rapture in ancient Bacchic revels."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "82cb194c-47d6-40c9-a1ac-361d36c2171f",
                                "sense_id": "377497ad-e7fd-3697-9181-bc8f5eba1441",
                                "text": "Shall the warriors of Thebes be dumb? \"Euoi! Euoi! Hail Bacchus!\" They dance to the pipe and drum."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d5ca7885-8c95-4054-874d-d334cb70be1c",
                                "sense_id": "377497ad-e7fd-3697-9181-bc8f5eba1441",
                                "text": "Euoi! Curving vines, delicate tendrils from sinews and tendons. Euoi! Candle flames and sweet smoke sting, swarm with the sound of bees..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ce31fa8-b578-4416-941a-8d98c4f3e32c",
                                "sense_id": "377497ad-e7fd-3697-9181-bc8f5eba1441",
                                "text": "The Bacchic cry of Euoi is not too dissimilar to Jesus' penultimate cry, while on the cross, of Eloi, Eloi."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "908adac6-3182-49bc-a5fa-5aa15223fcca",
                                "sense_id": "377497ad-e7fd-3697-9181-bc8f5eba1441",
                                "text": "[…] sexually aroused by them but never successful in their urge to debauch them. The maenads, Diodoros continues, cry out 'euoi' […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
